# Sanity

Schema: `slug` (unique), `order`, inline `seo`, PT `body`, image `alt` (required for content images), parent `weak: false`

## GROQ (`queries.ts` only)

- Explicit fields (no top-level `...`)
- `slug { current }` · `seo { title, description }` (or project-specific SEO fields)
- Image projections include `alt` + dimensions/LQIP when used for LCP
- **Published content:** prefer `perspective: 'published'` on `sanity/lib/client.ts` when hardening — do **not** scatter `!(_id in path("drafts.**"))` into every query (existing queries omit it; match that pattern)
- Production `useCdn: true` serves published; local `useCdn: false` can include drafts until perspective is set

DRY: one query per concern — fragments in `queries.ts`, **route access only via** `fetchers.ts` `get*` (`16-dry.mdc`). Never call `safeFetch` from `app/` or `components/`.

## Client & CDN

- `sanity/lib/client.ts`: `useCdn: true` in production; `apiVersion` pinned (YYYY-MM-DD)
- Images: `urlFor` / helpers in `sanity/lib/image.ts` — `.auto('format')`, explicit widths, `sizes`
- DTOs in `lib/types/` — keep fetch return types aligned with GROQ projections
- Studio LTR fields (email/phone/URL): `LtrStringInput`

## Routes

- Dynamic CMS routes: `generateStaticParams` + `getAll*Paths()` / `staticParamsFromPaths` (`lib/paths.ts`)
- Missing doc → `notFound()`; `revalidate = 300` on public CMS pages

## Cache & revalidation

- All `safeFetch` calls (inside fetchers only) tag **`cms`** — authority: `lib/cache-tags.ts`
- Prefer type tags: `cmsTypeTag('course')` · slug tags when invalidating one leaf
- ISR fallback: `revalidate = 300` on public routes
- On-demand: Sanity webhook → `/api/revalidate` — skill: **`setup-revalidation`**
- Webhook filter, path map, new `_type` handling → this rule + `app/api/revalidate/route.ts`
- Secret query param & env → **`17-security.mdc`** (do not duplicate auth rules here)

```ts
// In page.tsx — fetchers only
const data = await getThingBySlug(slug)
if (!data) notFound()
```

Workflow: `add-sanity-query` → `add-fetcher` → route skills (`new-page` / `new-leaf-route`).
